  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0043_a8af7c5d28fd.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 199px;\" /></p><p>As the speed is constant, only centripetal acceleration will act(towards the centre of the circular path),&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;towards the centre which at the given time will be towards right, hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Velocity of the particle at this instant will in upward direction and hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>v</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p>"
